import{_ as t,o as i,c as a,a2 as r}from"./chunks/framework.B3-dzFNu.js";const p=JSON.parse('{"title":"Model execution benchmark","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"model-execution-benchmark.md","filePath":"model-execution-benchmark.md","lastUpdated":1793496711000}'),o={name:"model-execution-benchmark.md"};function s(n,e,d,l,c,h){return i(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[r('<h1 id="model-execution-benchmark" tabindex="-1">Model execution benchmark <a class="header-anchor" href="#model-execution-benchmark" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Model execution benchmark&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Redline records the Pi execution-policy comparison under <code>benchmark/model-execution/v1/</code>. The checked-in live capture uses <code>z-ai/glm-5.3-flash</code> through OpenRouter, the four-fixture review-quality corpus, temperature <code>0</code>, and three repetitions per mode. Each mode therefore covers 12 fixture executions.</p><p>The benchmark compares:</p><ul><li>thinking levels <code>off</code>, <code>minimal</code>, and <code>low</code> with a 4,096-token output cap;</li><li><code>off</code> with 4,096 and 16,384 output tokens;</li><li>an OpenAI-compatible JSON response-format probe;</li><li>token usage and estimated cost;</li><li>local fresh-process overhead;</li><li>validated finding coverage and expected-issue evidence locations.</li></ul><h2 id="commands" tabindex="-1">Commands <a class="header-anchor" href="#commands" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Commands&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Regenerate the report from the checked-in capture:</p><div class="language-sh vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">sh</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;">mise</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> run</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> benchmark:model-execution</span></span></code></pre></div><p>The historical matrix includes reasoning-off profiles. These remain readable for deterministic replay, but the executor now rejects reasoning-off execution. Do not rerun that live matrix unchanged; a new live comparison must preserve the owner&#39;s reasoning decisions. Existing captures are not new measurements under the current policy.</p><h2 id="recorded-result" tabindex="-1">Recorded result <a class="header-anchor" href="#recorded-result" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Recorded result&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Mode</th><th style="text-align:right;">Complete fixtures</th><th style="text-align:right;">Expected issues credited</th><th style="text-align:right;">p95 per-fixture wall time</th><th style="text-align:right;">Output tokens</th><th style="text-align:right;">Estimated cost</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>off-4096</code></td><td style="text-align:right;">7/12</td><td style="text-align:right;">1/6</td><td style="text-align:right;">38,422 ms</td><td style="text-align:right;">28,917</td><td style="text-align:right;">$0.017678</td></tr><tr><td><code>minimal-4096</code></td><td style="text-align:right;">8/12</td><td style="text-align:right;">2/6</td><td style="text-align:right;">6,433 ms</td><td style="text-align:right;">6,073</td><td style="text-align:right;">$0.007792</td></tr><tr><td><code>low-4096</code></td><td style="text-align:right;">8/12</td><td style="text-align:right;">2/6</td><td style="text-align:right;">6,304 ms</td><td style="text-align:right;">5,711</td><td style="text-align:right;">$0.007057</td></tr><tr><td><code>off-16384</code></td><td style="text-align:right;"><strong>9/12</strong></td><td style="text-align:right;"><strong>3/6</strong></td><td style="text-align:right;">58,859 ms</td><td style="text-align:right;">23,578</td><td style="text-align:right;">$0.015161</td></tr><tr><td><code>off-4096-json</code></td><td style="text-align:right;">8/12</td><td style="text-align:right;">2/6</td><td style="text-align:right;">32,408 ms</td><td style="text-align:right;">25,676</td><td style="text-align:right;">$0.016071</td></tr></tbody></table><p>No mode introduced a validated false positive. The live provider still omitted files in every mode. Therefore, this capture is not an absolute quality pass. It is a relative policy comparison.</p><p><code>off-16384</code> had the best repeated completion and expected-issue credit counts in this historical capture. That result does not authorize disabling reasoning. Current production uses:</p><ul><li>model/provider-default reasoning, without a reasoning-disable override;</li><li>a 16,384-token default output cap; local CLI users can override it with <code>--max-output-tokens</code>, and the review environment accepts <code>REDLINE_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS</code>. The historical benchmark selected a default, not a universal model limit;</li><li>provider-default sampling in production (temperature <code>0</code> is a benchmark control only);</li><li>normal JSON text output, not provider-native response formatting.</li></ul><p>The JSON response-format probe did not improve coverage and is not portable across all supported OpenAI-compatible endpoints.</p><h2 id="deadlines-and-retries" tabindex="-1">Deadlines and retries <a class="header-anchor" href="#deadlines-and-retries" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Deadlines and retries&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The production action separates two deadlines:</p><ul><li><code>timeout</code>: 4 minutes per file;</li><li><code>run-timeout</code>: 10 minutes for the complete review.</li></ul><p>Each harness call receives the lesser of the per-file deadline and the remaining run budget. After the whole-run deadline expires, Redline starts no new model call. Every remaining reviewed file gets a deterministic <code>run-deadline-exhausted</code> omission. Summary artifacts record both deadlines, elapsed time, deadline status, and omission count.</p><p>Pi&#39;s internal retries are disabled. Redline permits one retry only for a classified transient empty provider response or a bounded transient HTTP or transport failure. The retry uses a fresh invocation directory and the same total file deadline. Redline does not retry timeouts, token-budget exhaustion, malformed output, parser failures, or validation failures.</p><h2 id="process-reuse-decision" tabindex="-1">Process reuse decision <a class="header-anchor" href="#process-reuse-decision" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Process reuse decision&quot;">​</a></h2><p>A ten-sample local probe measured fresh Pi process execution at 173 ms p50 and 211 ms p95, including Pi startup, configuration loading, a loopback streamed response, and JSON event extraction.</p><p>Fresh processes remain selected because they preserve the current per-file configuration, session, queue, tool, and credential boundary. Pi RPC is not selected because the current protocol does not prove a complete reset of all mutable state between untrusted files. Direct SDK execution is not selected because the production action intentionally installs no project dependencies; adding the SDK would expand the trusted runtime and credential surface without a measured model-bound benefit.</p><h2 id="artifact-safety" tabindex="-1">Artifact safety <a class="header-anchor" href="#artifact-safety" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Artifact safety&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The capture stores validated file records and bounded numeric telemetry only. It does not store prompts, source payloads, raw model output, reasoning, credentials, or publication tokens.</p><p>This benchmark does not satisfy the epic&#39;s live latency gate. Five eligible fixed-corpus SLO runs are still required.</p>',25)])])}const m=t(o,[["render",s]]);export{p as __pageData,m as default};
